    {
      "filename": "1947 Nanhai Zhudao.png",
      "title": "File:1947 Nanhai Zhudao.png",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/1947_Nanhai_Zhudao.png",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1947_Nanhai_Zhudao.png",
      "width": 2654,
      "height": 3840,
      "mime": "image/png",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Secretariat of Government of Guangdong Province, Republic of China",
      "credit": "Made by Territory Department of Ministry of the Interior, printed by Bereau of Surveying of Ministry of Defence.\n\nNow in Sun Yat-sen Library of Guangdong Province, China, this map describes Dongsha Islands, Xisha Islands and Zhongsha Islands in details. Every island has its name in Chinese and English, with depth of sea marks and descriptions as following:",
      "source": "1947 Nanhai Zhudao",
      "description": "Location Map of South China Sea Islands, Secretariat of Government of Guangdong Province. January, 1947. \nLeft margin written as: Made by Territory Department of Ministry of the Interior, printed by Bereau of Surveying of Ministry of Defence.\nNow in Sun Yat-sen Library of Guangdong Province, China, this map describes Dongsha Islands, Xisha Islands and Zhongsha Islands in details. Every island has its name in Chinese and English, with depth of sea marks and descriptions as following:\n\n\"November of 35th year of the Republic (A.D. 1946), Executive Yuan ordered the Navy Command Headquarter and Ministry of the Interior to assist Guangdong government to accept Nanhai Zhudao: ROCS Taiping, ROCS Zhongye to accept Tuansha Qundao, ROCS Yongxing, ROCS Zhongjian to accept Xisha Qundao. The mission is completed in December of the same year. In honor of the actions of Taiping Ship and Yongxing ship, Chang Island (長島) is renamed to Taiping Island (太平島), and the Lin Island (林島) is renamed to Yongxing Island (永興島) under orders. The Xiniao Island (西鳥島) is also called Spratly Island. Because it is located in the far south, so the Goverment renames it to Nanwei Island (南威島). The Ministry of the Interior adjusted the names of the islands according to their locations in the South China Sea, so changed Tuansha Islands (團沙群島) (i.e. Xinnan Islands (新南群島) by Japanese, Spratly Islands by Westerners) to Nansha Islands (南沙群島), and the former Japanese Nansha Islands (南沙群島) is renamed to Zhongsha Islands (中沙群島). The other islands and reefs are named after the historical diplomats to the Nanyang, in memory of them.\"",
      "dateCreated": "1947",
      "categories": [
        "20th-century maps of the South China Sea",
        "Files allowed to be overwritten by everyone",
        "Files in need of review (sources)",
        "Old maps of the Republic of China (1912–1949)",
        "PD-1996",
        "PD China"
      ],
